    <bpmn:process id="W_W3638" name="W3638. Measurement System Analysis (MSA) &amp; Gage R&amp;R" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New/critical measurement process; quality/acceptance concern; OOT trend
Frequency: Per measurement process + periodic
Volume: Critical measurement systems (quality, acceptance, cut-length, dispensing)
Owner: Metrology Manager / Quality
Participants: Metrology Manager, Quality (links to VS-31), Calibration Technicians (W3622), Device Operators, Process Owners, Statistics/BI (links to VS-28)
Source: workflow W3638 — Measurement System Analysis (MSA) &amp; Gage R&amp;R</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3638_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3638_Lane1" name="Metrology Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3638_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3638_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3638_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3638_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3638_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3638_Start3" name="New/critical measurement process; quality/acceptance concern; OOT trend">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3638_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3638_Task4" name="Metrology Manager/Quality conduct Measurement System Analysis (MSA) on critical…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Metrology Manager/Quality conduct Measurement System Analysis (MSA) on critical measurement systems: bias, linearity, stability, and repeatability &amp; reproducibility (Gage R&amp;R — the variation from the measurement system vs. the process); identify whether the measurement system is fit for acceptance decisions (% study variation, ndc)
Responsible (R): Metrology Manager / Quality / Statistics
Accountable (A): Quality Manager
Duration: Per process</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3638_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3638_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3638_Task5" name="Metrology Manager/Quality act on MSA findings: if the measurement system…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Metrology Manager/Quality act on MSA findings: if the measurement system contributes excessive variation, address device (calibration/repair W3634), method (procedure), operator (training W3623), environment, or standard; re-run MSA to confirm improvement
Responsible (R): Metrology Manager / Quality / Technicians
Accountable (A): Quality Manager
Duration: Per process</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3638_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3638_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3638_Task6" name="Metrology Manager integrate MSA into the quality/acceptance design (links to…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Metrology Manager integrate MSA into the quality/acceptance design (links to VS-31): ensure measurement systems underlying product acceptance, cut-length charge, and dispensing are validated for their decision; maintain MSA records (W3624) and report to governance (W3640) and quality audit (links to VS-31/VS-21)
Responsible (R): Metrology Manager / Quality
Accountable (A): Quality Manager
Duration: Periodic</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3638_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3638_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3638_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3638_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-576 (ensure controlled execution — Weights &amp; Measures Compliance, MRM &amp; Measurement Analytics (PA-115.3).) | - operational: MSA and Gage R&amp;R; operational: periodic re-validation
Owner: Metrology Manager / Quality</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
